{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792486919,"nonce":"w9v7ynrQJjAZxhfcBV4bNYdZISc=","message":"Implemented unconstrained generic function declarations and calls with inferred or explicit type arguments. The frontend checks one symbolic body per declaration and sends TypedFunction type parameters plus TypedCall type arguments through shared HIR. Forward calls, inferred results, multiple parameters, nested generic calls, same-type recursion, primitives, strings and scalar-record aliases work. Readonly views propagate through inferred and explicit results, including opt-in checked-policy rejections. Frequent new caches use Fx hashing and interned identities.\n\nShared fixes required for correct native execution: declared parameters are now rigid TypeVarKind::Parameter values rather than inference holes, while each generic call substitutes its own arguments; lowering keeps those parameters symbolic; embed import resolution preserves a call's instantiated result instead of replacing it with the template result. The shared specializer now consumes owned templates and call type-argument vectors, caches one concrete body and ID per key, specializes nested calls with an iterative worklist, preserves attributes/calling conventions and removes non-executable templates. It avoids the prior duplicate generation of each body and does not rescan non-generic modules. No frontend AST-body cloning or dynamic boxing is used for specialization.\n\nRemoved pending/generic from KNOWN_FAILURES: the file shrank from nine entries to eight. Added sixteen reference-backed cases, all passing, without adding expected failures. Full pinned/native suite has 94 cases. Live TypeScript 6.0.2/Node comparison returned 172 PASS and 16 XFAIL across interpreter and Cranelift profiles, with no unexpected results. Report: /private/tmp/zynode-gaps-20261020.json. No timing or throughput claims are made.\n\nValidation: full zyntax_